 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Matched pair",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Both transistors are neighbouring die cut from one wafer, an intrinsically matched pair. Gain, VCE(sat) and VBE(sat) agree between the two within 2 %, and base-emitter voltage within 2 mV, at most. Nothing inside the package joins them: transistor 1 is B1, C1, E1 and transistor 2 is B2, C2, E2."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Uses",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Applications: current mirrors, differential amplifiers, instrumentation amplifiers and comparators."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Automotive grade",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "An automotive-compliant version, DMMT3904WQ, exists and is covered by its own datasheet."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Thermal rating",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "The 200 mW and 625 °C/W figures apply to the package as a whole, both transistors together, on the minimum pad layout in still air. Allowed dissipation holds at 200 mW to about 28 °C ambient, then falls in a straight line to zero at 150 °C."
  },
  {
